# Common Governance — Core

## Core Principle (Non-Negotiable)

**AI writes 100% of infrastructure code and configuration. Humans govern.**

Humans may: define requirements, design systems, review configurations, test and debug, approve PRs, instruct AI to modify infrastructure code, create/edit n8n workflows via UI.
Humans must NOT manually write infrastructure code but may create workflows in n8n UI.

## Standard AI Workflow (6 Steps)

1. **Human defines task** — objective, constraints, acceptance criteria, edge cases, non-functional requirements
2. **AI generates plan** — architecture plan, files to change, test plan, risk assessment
3. **AI writes infrastructure code** — small PR increments (1–3 workflows or focused config changes)
4. **AI writes tests** — unit tests mandatory, integration tests where applicable
5. **Human reviews** — logic correctness, safety, maintainability, readability, CI status
6. **Deploy & monitor** — staging/prod, logs, metrics, traces

## Mandatory Prompt Format (7 Sections)

Every AI request MUST include: Context, Objective, Constraints, Inputs/Outputs, Acceptance Criteria, Edge Cases, Test Requirements.

**No-Guessing Rule:** If uncertain → AI must ask questions before coding.
**No-Magic Rule:** AI must NOT introduce random frameworks, unnecessary abstractions, or new tools without approval.

## Branch Protection

- ❌ No direct push to main/master
- ✅ All changes via PR
- ✅ Human approval required

## If a request violates any rule → Refuse and explain the violation.
